                                "sense_id": "c86319a3-db53-309b-a26d-b0fdb90ed92a",
                                "text": "Hindostan was then parcelled out into twelve grand divisions, called soobahs, to each of which a viceroy was assigned, by the title of Soobahdar, corruptly written Soobah by European writers; for, soobah signifies province: many of these soobahs were in extent equal to large European kingdoms."
